# brittinho-backend — copy to `.env` and fill in. The `.env` never enters git.

# ===== Deployment =====
# Image tag. Never `latest`.
BACKEND_VERSION=1.2.0
# Everything this service owns:
#
#   analytics.db   visits and sessions
#   content.db     the site's own data — gallery, posts, comments, guestbox
#   gb_snaps/      guestbox tracking snapshots
#   media/         the image files themselves
#
# content.db and media/ are the genuinely irreplaceable part. Analytics is
# pruned at 180 days and losing it costs history; losing media/ costs the
# images. Make sure this path is in whatever snapshots the NAS runs.
#
# MIGRATING FROM THE BOT: analytics data currently lives inside the bot's
# volume, at <bot data>/analytics/. Copy the whole directory here — the .db AND
# its -wal and -shm files, plus gb_snaps/. Copying only the .db captures an
# incomplete snapshot; with the bot stopped, `sqlite3 analytics.db ".backup
# out.db"` is the safe way to do it.
BACKEND_DATA_HOST_PATH=/mnt/StorageHD1/configs/brittinho_backend/data

# ===== API =====
# Bearer token guarding /api/analytics/*. Must match ANALYTICS_API_KEY in the
# site's api/analytics/_config.php.
#
# Use a NEW value, not the bot's old API_SECRET_KEY. The two were the same
# string, and that shared secret was exactly the coupling this split removes.
# The bot no longer reads API_SECRET_KEY at all. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
API_KEY=

# Origins allowed by CORS. Comma-separated, no trailing slashes.
#
# The response still carries exactly one origin — that header cannot hold a
# list — so this is an allowlist, not a widening: a caller whose Origin is on
# the list gets its own back, and everyone else gets the first entry, which
# their browser then refuses. Keep brittinho.com first.
#
# localhost:3000 is here so `npm run dev` in the site repo can talk to the real
# API instead of rendering an empty gallery. It grants nothing: these endpoints
# are public reads, the admin routes still demand a bearer token the browser
# never holds, and no Access-Control-Allow-Credentials is ever sent.
SITE_ORIGIN=https://brittinho.com,http://localhost:3000

# Origin that media URLs are built against. No trailing slash.
#
# The pages live on brittinho.com and the image files live here, so a relative
# `/media/...` in an API response would resolve against the site and 404. It has
# to be absolute — and it does not belong in the database, or moving domains
# would mean rewriting every stored row.
#
# Leave empty ONLY in development, where the API and the page share an origin.
MEDIA_BASE=https://api.brittinho.com

# ===== Telegram alerts =====
# Fires when a watchlist rule or watch group matches a visit. Both together or
# both empty — the service refuses to start with only one, because
# half-configured alerting never errors and never delivers.
#
# These moved here from the bot's stack. Remove them from stacks/britticobot/.env.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
